@startuml
title PayLink - Sequence Diagram: Refund a Failed Payment

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantPadding 20
skinparam BoxPadding 10

' =========================================================
' PARTICIPANTS - EXACT ORDER
' =========================================================

actor Customer
participant PaymentOrchestrator
participant Payment
participant Wallet
participant BillerAdapter
participant "Biller\n(AquaCo)" as Biller
participant NotificationEventListener
participant NotificationProvider

' =========================================================
' SCENARIO 1 - DIRECT BILLER REFUSAL AND AUTOMATIC HOLD RELEASE
' =========================================================

== Scenario 1: Direct Biller Refusal & Automatic Hold Release (Hard Case 3) ==

note over PaymentOrchestrator, Wallet
    PRECONDITION:

    Payment is currently in SentToBiller state.

    totalAmount (bill + fee) is reserved
    through a HOLD LedgerEntry.

    Funds are held in Wallet and have not
    yet been captured or released.
end note

' Step 1 - Biller Refusal

Biller --> BillerAdapter : refused(errorCode, reason)
BillerAdapter --> PaymentOrchestrator : BillerPaymentResult(Failed, reason)

' Step 2 - Transition to Failed

PaymentOrchestrator -> Payment : fail()
Payment --> PaymentOrchestrator : SentToBiller -> Failed\n(PaymentTransition recorded)

' Step 3 - Release the Hold

PaymentOrchestrator -> Wallet : releaseHold(totalAmount, reference)
Wallet --> PaymentOrchestrator : RELEASE_HOLD LedgerEntry created

note over Wallet
    Ledger-based hold release:

    Held funds return to available balance
    through a RELEASE_HOLD LedgerEntry.

    No direct balance overwriting.
end note

PaymentOrchestrator -> PaymentOrchestrator : record AuditLog (who, when, why)

' Step 4 - Transition to Refunded

PaymentOrchestrator -> Payment : refund()
Payment --> PaymentOrchestrator : Failed -> Refunded\n(final state; PaymentTransition recorded)

note over Payment
    Refunded is a final payment state.
    The hold has already been released.
end note

' Step 5 - Customer Notification (Observer Pattern)

PaymentOrchestrator ->> NotificationEventListener : onPaymentFailed(payment)

NotificationEventListener -> NotificationProvider : send SMS (refusal reason)
NotificationEventListener -> NotificationProvider : send PUSH (refusal reason)

alt NotificationProvider available

    NotificationProvider --> NotificationEventListener : notifications accepted

else NotificationProvider unavailable

    NotificationProvider --> NotificationEventListener : delivery failure

    NotificationEventListener -> NotificationEventListener : schedule NotificationRetryCommand

    note over NotificationEventListener, NotificationProvider
        Retry failed notifications up to 3 times.

        After the final unsuccessful retry:
        mark notification as UNDELIVERED.

        Payment remains Refunded regardless
        of notification delivery status.
    end note

end

PaymentOrchestrator --> Customer : payment failed and funds refunded (clear reason)

' =========================================================
' SCENARIO 2 - UNKNOWN PAYMENT GUARD
' =========================================================

== Scenario 2: Unknown Payment Guard — NEVER Refunded Automatically ==

note over PaymentOrchestrator, Wallet
    PRECONDITION:

    Payment timed out after 10 seconds.
    Current state: Unknown.

    Funds MUST stay held in Wallet.
    No automatic release or refund is allowed.
end note

' Step 1 - Attempted Automatic Refund (Forbidden)

PaymentOrchestrator -> Payment : attempt auto-refund while Unknown (guard check)
Payment --> PaymentOrchestrator : rejected by UnknownStateHandler\n(Unknown -> Refunded NOT allowed)

note over PaymentOrchestrator, Wallet
    GUARD RULE:

    Unknown -> Refunded is forbidden.

    Funds remain held.
    Payment state remains Unknown.

    A refund is possible only after
    Unknown -> Failed -> Refunded.
end note

' Step 2 - Resolve Unknown Payment

alt RetryCommand / callback confirms payment OR nightly reconciliation finds payment

    ' Branch 1 - Biller Confirms Payment

    PaymentOrchestrator -> Payment : confirm()
    Payment --> PaymentOrchestrator : Unknown -> Completed\n(final state; PaymentTransition recorded)

    PaymentOrchestrator -> Wallet : captureHold(totalAmount, reference)
    Wallet --> PaymentOrchestrator : DEBIT LedgerEntry recorded

    note over Wallet
        Held amount is captured through
        a DEBIT LedgerEntry.

        No direct balance mutation.
    end note

    PaymentOrchestrator ->> NotificationEventListener : onPaymentCompleted(payment)

    note over PaymentOrchestrator, Payment
        Payment is Completed.
        Funds are captured, not refunded.
    end note

else RetryCommand / callback receives biller refusal OR nightly reconciliation finds no payment

    ' Branch 2 - Biller Refuses or Reconciliation Finds No Payment

    PaymentOrchestrator -> Payment : fail()
    Payment --> PaymentOrchestrator : Unknown -> Failed\n(PaymentTransition recorded)

    PaymentOrchestrator -> Wallet : releaseHold(totalAmount, reference)
    Wallet --> PaymentOrchestrator : RELEASE_HOLD LedgerEntry created

    note over Wallet
        Held funds return to available balance
        through a RELEASE_HOLD LedgerEntry.

        No direct balance mutation.
    end note

    PaymentOrchestrator -> PaymentOrchestrator : record AuditLog (who, when, why)

    PaymentOrchestrator -> Payment : refund()
    Payment --> PaymentOrchestrator : Failed -> Refunded\n(final state; PaymentTransition recorded)

    PaymentOrchestrator ->> NotificationEventListener : onPaymentFailed(payment)

    NotificationEventListener -> NotificationProvider : send SMS (refusal/refund reason)
    NotificationEventListener -> NotificationProvider : send PUSH (refusal/refund reason)

    PaymentOrchestrator --> Customer : payment failed after verification; hold released (Refunded)

end

@enduml
